  "id": "monoideism",
  "term": "monoideism",
  "definition": "Monoideism is a mental state in which attention stays fixed on one idea for an unusually sustained period, with a rigid or artificially concentrated quality. In this historical usage, it refers to abnormal fixity of attention rather than ordinary focused attention.",
